+# Claude Code Native Agent, Skill, Tool & Plugin Ecosystem Architecture
+
+> **Status:** PROPOSED ARCHITECTURE & GLOBAL DISCOVERY POLICY (`DEC-2026-11-17-02` — **PROPOSED, AWAITING OWNER APPROVAL; REVISED v2 INCORPORATING ADVERSARIAL AUDIT & INDEPENDENT REVIEW**).  
+> **Scope Boundary:** Cross-cutting development and orchestration ecosystem architecture for Claude Code (`vano1919/explainer-engine`). This specification preserves `P1.3` (`Read-only Production State and dependency snapshot`) as a strictly separate workstream and modifies zero `.py`, `.json`, or schema files until explicit Owner approval.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Strategic Decision, Precedence & Airtight `P1.3` Boundary
+
+1. **Primary Environment:** Explainer Engine is architected specifically for **Claude Code** ([official Skills documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills), [Subagents documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents), [Hooks reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks), [Plugins overview](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/overview), [Plugin security](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/security)) as its primary development and episode-orchestration agent environment.
+2. **Native-First Design:** All project instructions (`CLAUDE.md`), path/domain rules (`.claude/rules/*.md`), on-demand Skills (`.claude/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md`), Subagents and stage pages (`.claude/agents/<name>.md`), deterministic lifecycle Hooks (`.claude/settings.json`), MCP server integrations (`.mcp.json`), and Plugins (`.claude-plugin/plugin.json` / `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`) are designed directly around Claude Code's native runtime semantics rather than a generic wrapper framework.
+3. **Open Standard Interoperability:** Project Skills conform to the open [Agent Skills Specification (`agentskills.io/specification`)](https://agentskills.io/specification) (`name`, `description`, `license`, `compatibility`, `metadata`, `allowed-tools`, and progressive disclosure across `SKILL.md`, `references/`, `scripts/`, and `assets/`) while leveraging Claude Code native extensions (`disable-model-invocation`, `user-invocable`, `argument-hint`, `model`, `effort`, `context: fork`, `agent`, `hooks`, `paths`, `shell`, dynamic `` !`cmd` `` context injection, `/skill-name` slash invocation, and subagent `skills` preloading) where beneficial.
+4. **Normative Boundary Clause Separating `DEC-2026-11-17-02` from Phase 1 `P1.3`:**
+   > **Binding Rule:** `DEC-2026-11-17-02` shall not define, modify, or own any episode-level production state, stage-state schema, job-state schema, timing contract, or runtime dependency snapshot contract belonging to `P1.3`. `P1.3` may reference approved component identifiers (`tool_id`, `skill_id`, `mcp_id`) and provenance metadata from the `DEC-2026-11-17-02` global tooling catalog, but remains independently specified and implemented in [MASTER_ARCHITECTURE_AND_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md](MASTER_ARCHITECTURE_AND_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md).
+
+| Responsibility / Concern | `DEC-2026-11-17-02` (Global Claude Code Ecosystem Catalog & Policy) | `P1.3` (`Read-only Production State & Dependency Snapshot`) |
+|---|---|---|
+| **Claude Code Skills (`.claude/skills/*`)** | **Yes** (discovery, rubric, `computedHash`, lifecycle state) | **No** |
+| **Claude Plugins, Marketplaces & MCP Servers** | **Yes** (trust tier, `SP-1..SP-6` security profile, hook matchers) | **No** |
+| **Agent & Subagent Governance (`.claude/agents/*`)** | **Yes** (`model_routing.json` role locks, `15,000`-token ceiling) | **No** |
+| **Global Tool Trust & Supply-Chain Provenance** | **Yes** (what tools/versions are *permitted* in the repository) | **No** |
+| **Episode Stage State (`episodes/<id>/production/stages/<stage>.json`)** | **No** | **Yes** (sole owner) |
+| **Job State (`jobs/<id>/state.json`, `job_manifest.json`)** | **No** | **Yes** (sole owner) |
+| **Episode Timing (`audio/timing.json`, `clock_sha256`)** | **No** (governed by `P1.1`/`P1.2` `DEC-2026-11-17-01`) | **Yes** (reads/snapshots dependency state) |
+| **Runtime Dependency Snapshot for an Episode Run** | **No** (provides static catalog IDs only) | **Yes** (captures live runtime versions/hashes actually used by an episode) |
+| **Episode Execution Evidence & Stale-Stage Detection** | **No** | **Yes** (sole owner) |
