+## 3. Claude Code Native Component Architecture & Official Runtime Semantics
+
+| Component Layer | Canonical Location | Primary Responsibility & Official Runtime Semantics | What It Must NEVER Do |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| **A. `CLAUDE.md` & `.claude/rules/`** | `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/rules/*.md` | Always-loaded architectural invariants, source-of-truth order, approval gates, budget/security fences, and concise routing pointers (`< 200` lines target per file) | Must not inline 500-line procedural manuals, tool recipe tables, or per-shot prompt templates |
+| **B. Project Skills (`SKILL.md`)** | `.claude/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md` (+ `references/`, `scripts/`, `assets/`, `evals/`) | On-demand procedural workflows ([`code.claude.com/docs/en/skills`](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills)): `~100` tokens metadata at startup; `< 5,000` tokens / `< 500` lines body on activation; supports `disable-model-invocation: true`, `` !`cmd` `` preprocessing, `/cd` loading (`v2.1.246+`), and worktree root fallback (`v2.1.277+`). Reserved names (`synced`, `anthropic-skills`) are forbidden. | Must not claim to install/connect an executable Tool, instruct destructive shell commands without `SP-2` review, or bypass `spend_caps.json` / `.claude/settings.json` hooks |
+| **C. Subagents & Stage Pages** | `.claude/agents/<name>.md` (governed by `config/model_routing.json`) | Context isolation ([`code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents`](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents)) for high-volume read-only exploration, independent fresh-eyes critique (`script-critic`, `youtube-viewer-critic`), or stage-locked checklists (`stage_guard`). Combined descriptions must remain well below Claude Code's `15,000`-token startup warning (`v2.1.271+` supports `omitClaudeMd: true`; `v2.1.296+` supports `autoCompactWindow`). | Must not violate the single-spawner/read-only-critic lock in `tests/unit/test_agent_roles.py`, trigger unapproved `multi-agent-analysis` (`"only on the creator's word (part 5)"`), or mutate files from a critic |
+| **D. Lifecycle Hooks** | `.claude/settings.json` -> `explainer_engine/{governance,cloud,standards}/hooks.py` | Deterministic pre/post policy gates ([`code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks`](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks)): exit `0` allows, exit `2` (or JSON `permissionDecision: "deny"`) blocks. Must use `Bash|Monitor` (`v2.1.314+`) to cover background monitor invocations, and `mcp__.*__.*` (plus explicit `mcp__<server>__.*` / `mcp__plugin_<plugin>_<server>__.*`) for MCP coverage. Security & spend hooks must enforce **fail-closed** (`onFailure: "block"` / `exit 2`). | Must not be treated as an OS/process sandbox once a script or binary starts executing; security/spend hooks must never fail open on internal exceptions |
+| **E. Executable Tools & MCP Servers** | `.mcp.json`, Python modules (`explainer_engine/**`, `tools/render_tools/**`), CLI binaries (`ffmpeg`, `ffprobe`, `blender`, `modal`) | Actual deterministic execution, file probing, rendering, schema validation, and external API/process transport | Must not embed unreviewed creative taste or execute billable cloud/API calls without passing repository gates |
+| **F. Claude Plugins & Marketplaces** | `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` | Versioned packaging unit ([`code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/manifest-reference`](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/manifest-reference)) when multi-repo distribution or immutable release pinning is required. Note: plugins do **not** load from `.claude/settings.json` in cloud sessions ([`code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/install`](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/install)). | Must not enable auto-updates, wrap every project Skill into a plugin, rely on plugin subagent `hooks`/`mcpServers`/`permissionMode` frontmatter (ignored by Claude Code), or ship unreviewed `bin/`, `monitors`, `mods`, or `lspServers` ([`code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/security`](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/security)) |
