+## 7. Central Registry Architecture (5 Normalized Linked Tables & Complete Hash Contract)
+
+To model the `1 Marketplace -> N Plugins -> N Skills / MCP Servers / Executable Tools` relationship cleanly without entity conflation, the central registry is normalized into **five linked tables** (`7.2.A` Marketplaces, `7.2.B` Plugins, `7.2.C` Skills, `7.2.D` MCP Servers, `7.2.E` Executable Tools) with explicit primary keys and foreign-key parent references (`parent_marketplace_id`, `parent_plugin_id`).
+
+### 7.1 Required Registry Fields, Complete `skill-hash.ts` Contract & Provenance Model
+
+#### A. Complete `skills-lock.json` v2 `computedHash` Contract (`kind == "skill"` Only)
+
+Per [`vercel-labs/skills/blob/main/src/skill-hash.ts`](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills/blob/main/src/skill-hash.ts), `skill_folder_computed_hash` applies **exclusively** to unpacked Skill directories and must obey all six normative rules when implemented in Python (`explainer-skills-lock-hasher`):
+1. **Recursive Walk & Exclusions:** Walk all files under the skill root directory, excluding `metadata.json`, `.git`, `__pycache__`, and `__pypackages__`.
+2. **Symlink Containment Gate:** Resolve any symbolic link's target realpath; **exclude (or reject) any symlink pointing outside the skill root directory** or forming a directory cycle.
+3. **Path Normalization & Byte-Order Sorting:** Convert relative file paths to forward-slash (`/`) form and sort all relative paths lexicographically by **raw UTF-8 byte value** (`path.encode("utf-8")`).
+4. **Line-Ending Normalization:** Normalize `
+` (`CRLF`) to `
+` (`LF`) across text file contents before measuring byte length.
+5. **Framing Format:** Feed `relative_path_utf8 + b"␀" + str(len(normalized_bytes)).encode("ascii") + b"␀" + normalized_bytes` into a single streaming `SHA-256` digest.
+6. **Output Format:** 64-character lowercase hexadecimal SHA-256 string.
+
+#### B. Six-Field Component-Specific Provenance Model
+
+Every registry entry records its unique primary key (`*_id`), optional foreign key (`parent_marketplace_id` / `parent_plugin_id`), `kind` (`marketplace` | `plugin` | `skill` | `mcp_server` | `executable_tool`), `functional_domain`, `security_profile` (`SP-1..SP-6`), `validation_profile` (`VP-1..VP-6`), and the six provenance fields:
+1. `source_git_sha_40`: Full 40-character Git commit SHA (or `NOT_VERIFIED_40CHAR (<7-char>)` prior to local clone).
+2. `release_tag_or_version`: SemVer release tag (`v2.0.0`, `v1.4.0`, `v3.10.1`, `v1.5.25`) or `N/A`.
+3. `skill_folder_computed_hash`: 64-char hex digest per Section 7.1.A (required when `kind == "skill"` and unpacked locally; `N/A` otherwise).
+4. `package_archive_sha256`: Tarball/zip SHA-256 or npm SHA-512 integrity digest (required when `kind == "plugin"`).
+5. `binary_or_image_digest`: Exact binary version constraint + local binary SHA-256 / container digest (for `kind in {"mcp_server", "executable_tool"}`).
+6. `first_party_repo_revision`: Local Git commit SHA (`eb80e4434ea120f48cb9aea094ebd7b2b423d8f0`) for tracked first-party files.
+
+### 7.2 Five-Table Normalized Registry Snapshot
+
+#### A. Marketplaces Registry (`kind = marketplace`, 1 -> N Plugins)
+
