+## 8. Capability-Based Validation Profiles (`VP-1..VP-6`) & Argon Guardrails (`AG-01..AG-08`)
+
+### 8.1 Capability-Based Risk Escalation Rule & Tiered Validation Profiles (`VP-1..VP-6`)
+
+**Binding Escalation Principle:** A component's Validation Profile is determined by its **actual effective capabilities and highest-risk instruction/execution surface**, never merely by its file extension or label:
+- A Markdown `SKILL.md` that instructs Claude to execute file-mutating or destructive `Bash` commands escalates from `VP-1` to **`VP-2`** (or **`VP-6`** if it instructs cloud/API calls).
+- A "read-only" MCP server that can read local filesystem paths, environment variables, or private credentials escalates to **`VP-4`** with strict path/secret deny rules.
+- A Plugin package (`VP-5`) automatically inherits the **highest validation profile (`max(VP)`)** of any Skill, Script, Hook, Monitor, Mod, LSP server, or MCP server bundled inside it.
+
+| Profile | Capability Classification | Required Evidence | Negative Tests (`$0.00` Local) | Positive Tests (`$0.00` Local) | Failure Behavior | Owner Approval Requirement | Exit Criteria (`SANDBOX VALIDATED` -> `PRODUCTION VALIDATED`) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **`VP-1`** | **Pure Informational / Advisory Skill or Rule** (`0` scripts, `0` `` !`cmd` `` shell directives, `0` destructive `Bash` instructions) | `SKILL.md` diff, `docs_lint` output, token count, `skill_folder_computed_hash` | `>= 5` near-miss prompts that must **not** trigger the skill; test rejecting reserved names (`synced`, `anthropic-skills`) and bodies `>= 500` lines | `>= 5` target prompts matching description; `pytest tests/unit/test_agent_governance.py tests/unit/test_t3_agent_skill_banners.py` | Fails build/lint (`exit 1`); skill not loaded | Required before committing to `.claude/` (`DEC-*` or thread approval) | `0` `docs_lint` findings, combined skill metadata `< 2,500` tokens, 1 dry-run task obeying `no_names` & `retired_era.json` |
+| **`VP-2`** | **Local Deterministic Script / CLI Tool / Action-Instructing Skill** (`scripts/*.py`, `explainer_engine/**`, `tools/render_tools/**`, or Skill invoking `Bash`) | AST security scan report, `--dry-run` output, `pytest` output, and (for media tools) rendered contact sheet + audio loudness report | Tests proving refusal (`exit != 0`) on missing inputs, existing output without `--overwrite`, invalid schema (`episode_timing/1` & `/2`), and millisecond drift | `--help`, `--dry-run --json` in `tmp_path` (`0` source files mutated), frame-exact `24fps` integer math tests | Refuses execution cleanly before writing output; removes partial files on `SIGTERM`/timeout | Required before adding/modifying production pipeline scripts | All unit tests green + **Mandatory Visual Contact-Sheet (`look.py`) & Audio QA (`AG-06`)** + fresh-context critic review |
