+### 8.2 Mandatory Argon Operational Guardrails (`AG-01`–`AG-08`)
+
+Derived directly from the repository's Argon/Opus/ChatGPT incident history (`docs/wip/argon_2026-11-14/09_OPUS_VERIFY_SESSION2.md`, `24_OPUS_VISUAL_CHECK_MAPS_S8.md`, `36_CHATGPT_REVIEW_OF_PLAN_R1.md`, `37_SLICE_REVIEW_1.md`, `INCIDENT_JOURNAL_argon_loop.md`) and reinforced by independent architectural review, every implementation agent and skill must obey eight non-negotiable engineering rules:
+- **`AG-01` (No `sys.modules` Leaks in Tests):** Never mutate `sys.modules[...]` directly or call private `monkeypatch._undo` in tests; always use `monkeypatch.setitem(sys.modules, name, fake)` and public APIs so full-suite `pytest` runs never poison downstream modules (`09_OPUS_VERIFY_SESSION2.md` Defect 1).
+- **`AG-02` (No Test-Accommodation Fallbacks in Production Code):** Never add production fallback branches (such as appending insert audio at the end of an unsplit read when timestamps are missing) just to make a stubbed unit test pass (`09_OPUS_VERIFY_SESSION2.md` Defect 2).
+- **`AG-03` (Generated Standards & `docs_lint` Sync):** Whenever `explainer_engine/standards/sourced_rules.json` is edited, immediately run both `python -m explainer_engine.standards.sourced_rules write` and `python -m explainer_engine.docs_lint` (`09_OPUS_VERIFY_SESSION2.md` Defect 3).
+- **`AG-04` (Schema Immutability During Data/Episode Fixes):** Never weaken or loosen a JSON Schema in `explainer_engine/schemas/` (e.g., permitting `motion_imitation` on `video` shots) to silence a validation error in an episode data file; fix the episode data (`37_SLICE_REVIEW_1.md` R1).
+- **`AG-05` (Preserve JSON Formatting & Avoid Bulk Template Slop):** Never run whole-file `json.dumps(..., indent=2)` rewrites that create 30,000-line diffs across `production_script.json`, and never substitute generic template loops for shot-specific creative direction (`INCIDENT_JOURNAL_argon_loop.md` 15:00 & 19:30).
+- **`AG-06` (Synthetic Tests != Visual or Audio Quality — Mandatory Dual Media QA):** Passing `pytest` checks structural invariants only.
+  - **Visual QA:** Any change affecting maps, snow/steam/fire overlays, 2.5D parallax, framing, or transitions must be verified by rendering and inspecting multi-frame contact sheets (`look.py`, checking frames `0`, `25%`, `50%`, `75%`, `last` per `37_SLICE_REVIEW_1.md` V1–V6).
+  - **Audio QA:** Contact sheets do not test sound. Any change affecting TTS, SFX, stem mixing, ducking, or `retime_with_edit_points()` must be verified on real rendered WAV/MP3 outputs for: (1) actual audio playback inspection, (2) true-peak clipping and EBU R128 integrated LUFS loudness compliance, (3) word/cut synchronization against `episode_timing`, (4) narration-to-music/ambience ducking balance, and (5) absence of unexpected silence or gaps.
+- **`AG-07` (Evidence Integrity — Zero Unverified Pass Claims):** An agent must **never** claim `Test PASS`, `Build SUCCESS`, `Visual PASS`, or `Integration PASS` unless the exact verification command was executed in the current working tree state. Every pass claim must include the verbatim command executed, exit code, and output summary line (`INCIDENT_JOURNAL_argon_loop.md` 15:00 `KeyError: 'rows'` lesson).
+- **`AG-08` (Change Scope Discipline):** Strictly forbidden in any task: (1) concurrent edits to the same file by multiple independent agents, (2) mass formatting of unrelated files, (3) deleting, skipping, or weakening existing unit tests solely to obtain a green test run, and (4) out-of-scope refactoring beyond the approved Task Contract.
