+## 9. Component-Specific Security Profiles (`SP-1..SP-6`), Complete Plugin Surface Controls & Fail-Closed Enforcement
+
+### 9.1 Eight Plugin Execution Surfaces, Universal Matchers & Fail-Closed Policy
+
+**Critical Security Distinction:** Claude Code `.claude/settings.json` `PreToolUse` hooks inspect the **tool invocation envelope** before execution. Once a `PreToolUse` hook exits `0` to allow a `Bash` command, Python script, or local MCP tool call, **hooks provide zero OS-level filesystem, network, environment-variable, or child-process sandboxing**.
+
+Per [Claude Code Plugin Security](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/security), [Plugins Components Reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/components), and [Hooks Reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks), third-party plugins and extensions expose **eight distinct security and execution surfaces** that must be governed:
+1. **`hooks/hooks.json`:** Lifecycle shell commands executed with user permissions.
+2. **`monitors`:** Background shell commands started automatically at session start, plugin reload, or skill invocation. Note per [Claude Code Hooks Reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks): a `PreToolUse` hook with only `"matcher": "Bash"` may fire on a `Monitor` command, but `allow` and `updatedInput` have no effect unless the matcher explicitly includes `Monitor` (**`"matcher": "Bash|Monitor"`**, supported in `v2.1.314+`).
+3. **`mods`:** JavaScript modules running directly inside Claude Code's own process with full user permissions.
+4. **`mcpServers`:** Local stdio or remote HTTP servers whose tools are prefixed `mcp__plugin_<plugin-name>_<server-name>__<tool>` (bypassing single-server `mcp__<server>__.*` matchers unless covered by `mcp__plugin_<plugin>_<server>__.*` or the universal MCP matcher **`mcp__.*__.*`**).
+5. **`bin/` directory:** Executables automatically prepended to the `Bash` tool's `PATH` when the plugin is enabled.
+6. **`lspServers` (`.lsp.json`):** Language Server Protocol binaries/processes spawned automatically when opening matching file types.
+7. **Instruction Surfaces (`skills/`, `commands/`, `agents/`):** Prompt instructions and `` !`cmd` `` directives that steer Claude's tool invocations (while plugin subagents silently ignore `hooks`, `mcpServers`, and `permissionMode` frontmatter).
+8. **Auto-Updates:** Remote marketplace/plugin auto-updates that can silently mutate audited files after initial review unless auto-update is hard-disabled and assets are vendored (`--copy`) with pinned hashes.
+
+#### Mandatory Hook Failure Policy (`Fail-Closed` vs. `Fail-Open`)
+
+Currently, `explainer_engine/governance/hooks.py` L22 states that hooks fail open (`exit 0`) on internal Python exceptions. Under `DEC-2026-11-17-02`, hook error handling is split into two strict categories (paired with Claude Code's `onFailure: "block"` setting on security/spend hooks, verified against the active runtime version):
+
+| Hook Purpose / Category | Examples in Repository | Mandatory Exception & Timeout Policy |
+|---|---|---|
+| **Security Enforcement** | Protected config writes (`pre-write`), force-push / `branch -D` without backup (`pre-bash`), unauthorized MCP/Monitor calls (`Bash|Monitor`, `mcp__.*__.*`) | **`Fail-Closed` (`exit 2` + `onFailure: "block"`):** Any unhandled exception, malformed payload, or timeout blocks the tool call immediately. |
+| **Spend Authorization** | RunPod/Modal/Hyperstack launch gates (`explainer_engine.cloud.hooks`), ElevenLabs paid generation (`explainer_engine.standards.hook`) | **`Fail-Closed` (`exit 2` + `onFailure: "block"`):** Any exception or missing `paid_offer/1` / `spend_caps.json` record blocks execution so zero unapproved money can be spent. |
+| **Logging / Telemetry** | `statusLine`, `PostModelSwitch` usage logging | **`Fail-Open` (`exit 0`):** Prints a 1-line diagnostic warning to stderr and allows the session to continue. |
+| **Informational Warning / Post-Edit Lint** | `UserPromptSubmit` reminder line, `PostToolUse` `post-edit` (`py_compile` / `docs_lint` feedback) | **`Fail-Open` (`exit 0`):** Reports lint findings back to Claude without deadlocking the editor. |
+
+### 9.2 Six Component-Specific Security Profiles (`SP-1` through `SP-6`)
+
+| Security Profile | Component Scope | Allowed Execution Surface | Mandatory Containment & Enforcement Controls |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| **`SP-1` — Pure Instruction Skill** | `.claude/skills/<name>/` containing only `.md` and static `.json` templates | Prompt context only (`0` executable files, `0` `` !`cmd` `` shell injections, `0` destructive `Bash` instructions) | Verify `find <skill_dir> -type f ! -name '*.md' ! -name '*.json'` is empty and `grep -rn '!\`' <skill_dir>` is empty; if a Markdown skill instructs destructive/billable `Bash` commands, escalate to `SP-2`/`SP-6`. |
+| **`SP-2` — Skill + Local Deterministic Script** | `.claude/skills/<name>/scripts/*.py` or `explainer_engine/**` CLI tools | Local Python 3.10+ stdlib + approved local binaries (`ffmpeg`, `ffprobe`) | 1. Static AST audit bans `urllib`, `requests`, `httpx`, `socket`, `subprocess(..., shell=True)`, and reads of `.env` / `vault.json` / `~/.ssh` / `~/.aws`.<br>2. Scripts must take explicit input/output paths, refuse overwriting inputs, and support `--dry-run`. |
+| **`SP-3` — Local Stdio MCP Server** | `.mcp.json` stdio process | Persistent local child process speaking JSON-RPC over stdio | 1. Launch with a sanitized environment (`env -i PATH=... HOME=...`, stripping cloud API keys).<br>2. Register fail-closed `.claude/settings.json` `PreToolUse` matchers using universal **`mcp__.*__.*`** plus explicit `mcp__<server>__.*` / `mcp__plugin_<plugin>_<server>__.*` (verified on the target Claude Code version). |
+| **`SP-4` — Remote HTTP MCP Server** | `.mcp.json` or Claude Connector HTTP endpoint | Outbound HTTPS JSON-RPC to named vendor domain | 1. Pure public docs endpoints (`mcp-hyperstack-docs`) allowed at `$0` only after verifying zero access to local files/secrets.<br>2. Any connector capable of reading private data or billing (`mcp-elevenlabs`, `mcp-hyperstack-console`) requires a fail-closed (`exit 2`, `onFailure: "block"`) `PreToolUse` hook under `mcp__.*__.*`. |
+| **`SP-5` — Full Claude Plugin Package** | `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` / `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` | Multi-component bundle audited across all **8 surfaces** | 1. **Hard ban** on third-party plugins containing `mods`, auto-starting `monitors`, `lspServers`, unreviewed `bin/` executables, or auto-updates.<br>2. Require `"matcher": "Bash|Monitor"` (`v2.1.314+`) in `PreToolUse` hooks so background monitor commands cannot bypass `Bash` restrictions.<br>3. Never place security-critical subagents inside a plugin (`hooks`, `mcpServers`, and `permissionMode` are ignored on plugin subagents).<br>4. Prefer vendoring vetted `SKILL.md` + `references/` (`--copy`) under `.claude/skills/` (`SP-1`/`SP-2`) over enabling full plugins. |
+| **`SP-6` — Billable Cloud / GPU / Paid API Tool** | `explainer_engine/cloud/*`, `modal`, `runpod`, `hyperstack`, paid `ElevenLabs` / `Gemini` / `BFL` / `fal` | External billable infrastructure | **Dual-Key Fail-Closed Defense in Depth:** Guarded simultaneously by (a) fail-closed `.claude/settings.json` `PreToolUse` hook (`Bash|Monitor` and `mcp__.*__.*`, `exit 2`, `onFailure: "block"`) **and** (b) trusted in-code worker preflight (`cheapest.py` `CH-01..CH-07`, `paid_offer/1`, `spend_caps.json`, and 60-minute `governance ok` creator-word verification stored in a trusted layer outside model-writable context). |
+
+### 9.3 Binding $0 Cost & Operational Invariants
+
+1. **Zero Paid Calls Without Dual Fail-Closed Gates (`SP-6`):** No Skill, Subagent, Plugin, or MCP server may initiate any paid API or GPU call without passing both the fail-closed `PreToolUse` hook and the in-code `spend_caps.json` / `paid_offer/1` preflight with explicit Owner approval.
+2. **No Automatic Installation or Auto-Update:** `npx skills update`, `/plugin update`, marketplace auto-updates, or unpinned `git pull` inside `.claude/` are forbidden. All third-party skills/plugins are copied (`--copy`) after review and pinned by `source_git_sha_40` + component-specific integrity hash.
+3. **Telemetry & Credential Hygiene:** Set `DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1` and `DO_NOT_TRACK=1` whenever running third-party discovery CLIs (`npx skills`), and never pass `.env`, `vault.json`, or API keys to external skill scripts or local stdio MCP servers.
